%% title: How a notice travels
%% desc: You write the notice and pick who gets it, then publish. People with the app see it in the app; an important one also stays in their warning bar until they press I've read it. If you ticked Public, a link is made and shown once. An SMS goes only after an admin approves it. You can withdraw the notice at any time, and its links stop working.
flowchart LR
  W["Write notice<br/>and pick people"] --> P["Publish"]
  P --> A["In the app:<br/>list and home card"]
  A --> I{"Important?"}
  I -- "Yes" --> B["Warning bar until<br/>I've read it"]
  I -- "No" --> N["Normal notice"]
  P --> L{"Public?"}
  L -- "Yes" --> K["Link shown once"]
  P --> S{"SMS asked?"}
  S -- "Yes" --> R["Admin looks,<br/>unticks people"]
  R --> D{"Approve?"}
  D -- "Approve" --> G["SMS sent,<br/>credits used"]:::done
  D -- "Decline" --> X["Nothing sent"]
  P --> Z["Withdraw any time:<br/>links stop"]
  classDef done fill:#ebfbee,stroke:#2b8a3e,color:#14411d
